SBW Drone Warfare — Fabric 1.21.1 port
=====================================

This repository is a fork of:

  [SBW] Drone Warfare
  https://github.com/SmartStreamLabs/-SBW-Drone-Warfare
  Upstream commit: 30e7b655e85301f7c3607d2279e8aad268dfa91d ("Changelog", 2026-06-24)
  Upstream version at that commit: 1.0.1 (Forge 1.20.1)
  Authors: Team SmartStreamLabs
  License: GNU Affero General Public License v3.0 (see LICENSE)

The `main` branch mirrors upstream unchanged. All Fabric port work lives on
the `fabric-1.21.1` branch.

Source base: the Fabric port is written on top of this fork (upstream 1.0.1 above). The later
upstream tree below was used only as a behavioural reference; no code or assets were imported from it.

Later upstream source (reference only, not merged):
  https://github.com/SmartStreamLabs/SBW-Drone-Warfare-Updated-8-28-2026
  commit 9eb3b598083838facc16022738aa06ad48fbfb04 (2026-08-28), AGPL-3.0,
  NeoForge 1.21.1 / version 1.0.6 sources are in SBW-Drone-Range-1.20.1.
  All 154 released assets match (9 after line-ending normalization), as do
  all 258 top-level class paths. See docs/PROVENANCE.md for verification limits.

Modifications
-------------
The Fabric port changes are made by netherg-io
(https://github.com/netherg-io) and contributors, and are licensed under the
same AGPL-3.0 terms. Per AGPL-3.0 §5(a), changes are recorded with dates:

  2026-09-14  Fork created. Added NOTICE, CREDITS.md, README.md; upstream
              README moved to README-upstream.md. No code or asset changes.

  2026-09-24  Added isolated Fabric build, registry and FPV prototype based on
              public superbwarfare-fabric bf18. Forge sources/resources are not
              included in the Fabric jar. See docs/PROVENANCE.md.

  2026-09-24  bf1 and before: server-side quadcopter flight (Angle/Acro), frame-locked
              FPV camera, payload mass, battery, armed contact fuze, radio link with
              obstruction and jamming, fibre-optic variant, motor sound.
  2026-09-25  bf2-bf4: pilot keeps the drone beyond view distance, 1 HP frame and damage
              attribution, observer attitude smoothing, session resync and lifecycle
              cleanup (disconnect, round end, room close), own item icons, fibre cut by
              players and spool reuse, Doppler and Sound Physics muffling, drones exempt
              from Entity Culling, camera restored when the monitor is taken away.
  2026-09-25  Built against superbwarfare-fabric bf19.

The full modification history is the git history of the `fabric-1.21.1` branch.

Third-party assets are listed with their source and license status in
CREDITS.md. Assets under non-commercial licenses (e.g. CC BY-NC-SA) are not
included in this port.

